The [original incident](/kb/incidents/4471) records one known issue and one queued fix.
The exported evidence separates it into two causes plus a separate anomaly investigation.

## Count the reports, not the intake guess

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The table deduplicates reports by ID, keeps only reports merged into #4471, and classifies
them from the tenant locale, booking form, and channel. The intake tag is only a guess.

## Two tickets

- **379 reports**: the shared parser reads dates month-first for day-first tenants. See
  [issue #1](https://github.com/piotrowczareknext/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1).
- **33 reports**: booking-v3 shows an `MM/DD/YYYY` hint to day-first tenants, conflicting
  with the tenant's date order. See
  [issue #2](https://github.com/piotrowczareknext/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2).
- **5 reports**: the desk notes flag a one-day move or other anomaly that is not proven to
  be either cause. These are a subset of the parser group, not an extra total; investigate
  them separately in [issue #3](https://github.com/piotrowczareknext/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/3).

<Callout>
Keep the parser, booking-v3 hint, and one-day anomaly investigations separate. The intake tag
and subject do not establish cause.
</Callout>

